---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import { capabilities, checked, features, formatDate, providers, useCases } from "../lib/data";
---

<Base title="About" description="Who runs Botperch, how it is kept current, what it does not do, and how to correct it.">
  <PageHeader
    kicker="About"
    title="About Botperch"
    standfirst="Botperch is an independent guide to where an AI agent can live: which cloud sandbox, virtual machine or server fits the job, what it costs, and the catch."
    meta={[`${providers.length} providers`, `Prices checked ${formatDate(checked.prices)}`, "Code and data public"]}
  />

  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="section section--flush">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Who runs it</h2>
        <p>
          Botperch is built and maintained by <a href="https://github.com/WyrdWerk">WyrdWerk</a>. The site's code and every
          data file are public in the <a href="https://github.com/WyrdWerk/sandbox-guide">sandbox-guide repository</a>,
          so any number on a page can be traced to the file it came from.
        </p>
        <p>
          Yash writes this guide at WyrdWerk. Find him as{" "}
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/yash-jain-65295511b/" rel="noreferrer noopener me">Yash on LinkedIn</a> and{" "}
          <a href="https://x.com/thelaggingway" rel="noreferrer noopener me">Yash on X</a>, and the company at{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/WyrdWerk" rel="noreferrer noopener">WyrdWerk on GitHub</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What it covers</h2>
        <p>
          {providers.length} providers, {features.length} features, {capabilities.length} specific capabilities checked for every
          provider, and {useCases.length} guides that start from what you want to run, from a personal agent to a remote MCP server.
          Costs come from one calculator that shows its arithmetic; <a href="/costs/how-it-works/">here is how it works</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>How it stays current</h2>
        <p>
          Each provider's prices are re-read from its own pricing page on a weekly schedule, and a person reviews every
          change before it is published. Every page shows the date its facts were checked, and dated changes at each
          provider are listed on <a href="/changes/">what changed</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What it does not do</h2>
        <p>
          The guide carries no ads and no affiliate links. It is desk research: no provider account was created and no
          sandbox was started or billed, so every statement about behaviour is what the provider documents, not something
          measured. Where a provider publishes nothing, the page says “not published” rather than guessing.
          <a href="/how-we-checked/">How we checked</a> has the full method and its limits.
        </p>

        <h2>Corrections</h2>
        <p>
          If a price or a claim is wrong, use the “Report something wrong” link at the foot of any page, or
          <a href="https://github.com/WyrdWerk/sandbox-guide/issues">open an issue</a> with a link to the provider's own page.
        </p>

        <h2>For AI agents</h2>
        <p>
          The same facts are available as plain files: start at <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>, or fetch
          <a href="/data/index.json">the provider index</a> and <a href="/llms-full.txt">everything in one file</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
